has the ability to do
so, and Facebook sure,

00:20:04.657 --> 00:20:05.766
you can go back.

00:20:05.766 --> 00:20:08.143
The posts don't get deleted
like they would on SnapChat

00:20:08.143 --> 00:20:11.626
but you don't really go
back on a Facebook post

00:20:11.626 --> 00:20:12.601
from five years ago.

00:20:12.601 --> 00:20:15.161
You don't go back on Facebook
posts from two days ago,

00:20:15.161 --> 00:20:18.894
and so I don't like that rush.

00:20:18.894 --> 00:20:21.157
So I think with Facebook,
if you had equal size

00:20:21.157 --> 00:20:24.713
audiences on both, you'll
get more instant views

00:20:24.713 --> 00:20:27.192
on Facebook, especially if
you do and you kind of boost

00:20:27.192 --> 00:20:30.777
around it to your audience,
but you'll get way longer

00:20:30.777 --> 00:20:32.667
term impact if you're on YouTube,

00:20:32.667 --> 00:20:34.477
and so that's the game.

00:20:34.477 --> 00:20:36.599
I don't care about hitting
everybody tomorrow,

00:20:36.599 --> 00:20:38.468
but I want people to be changed.

00:20:38.468 --> 00:20:39.983
I'm in this for the long run,

00:20:39.983 --> 00:20:41.973
and so YouTube is a better place for me.

00:20:41.973 --> 00:20:44.949
YL Mompreneurs, "Has this
been 100% organic growth

00:20:44.949 --> 00:20:47.936
"or have you used sponsored
posts/ads in the mix as well?"

00:20:47.936 --> 00:20:51.982
It's not 99.7% organic growth.

00:20:51.982 --> 00:20:54.896
We've done some targeted ads
based around certain videos

00:20:54.896 --> 00:20:57.142
to help give them a
little bit more exposure,

00:20:57.142 --> 00:21:01.496
but from my experience in
every campaign that I've run,

00:21:01.496 --> 00:21:04.811
you can get views from advertising,

00:21:04.811 --> 00:21:06.649
but you can't get subscribers.

00:21:06.649 --> 00:21:10.276
Subscribers don't convert a
lot from the views on videos,

00:21:10.276 --> 00:21:12.796
at least from my experience
in every ad that I've run,

00:21:12.796 --> 00:21:15.997
and so we don't make that a priority.

00:21:15.997 --> 00:21:17.530
If there's one video that
we're just trying to get

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:19.416
some awareness that
helps with the branding,

00:21:19.416 --> 00:21:21.410
something like that,
then we may run a couple

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:25.028
of campaigns, but in terms
of driving subscriber growth,

00:21:25.028 --> 00:21:29.347
it's almost zero, which sucks

00:21:29.347 --> 00:21:32.154
but if you do the work
on the organic side,

00:21:32.154 --> 00:21:34.579
you make really good stuff,
the people want to share,

00:21:34.579 --> 00:21:35.931
where they watch the
video, and they're like,

00:21:35.931 --> 00:21:37.541
that was amazing, I'm going
to subscribe to the channel

00:21:37.541 --> 00:21:39.816
and tell my friends about it,
then you can get the growth.

00:21:39.816 --> 00:21:43.906
So almost 100% of my growth has been

00:21:43.906 --> 00:21:47.156
just from organic and
doing things like this

00:21:47.156 --> 00:21:49.078
of understanding the YouTube algorithm

00:21:49.078 --> 00:21:51.423
to get as much exposure as possible.

00:21:51.423 --> 00:21:53.324
Pump Iron is asking,
"Evan, I love your videos.

00:21:53.324 --> 00:21:55.722
"My question is how do I
make money on YouTube?"

00:21:55.722 --> 00:21:57.335
That may be a future video.

00:21:57.335 --> 00:21:59.977
I don't know, we'll see if I
cover that on a standalone.

00:21:59.977 --> 00:22:02.223
I've done this already
on my channel, besides,

00:22:02.223 --> 00:22:04.484
I think the way to get started initially

00:22:04.484 --> 00:22:06.510
if you're just starting up as a YouTuber,

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:08.205
you'll make a little bit of money off of

00:22:08.205 --> 00:22:09.924
the AdSense that comes in.

00:22:09.924 --> 00:22:11.801
The key though as you're making more money

00:22:11.801 --> 00:22:13.427
will come when you have an audience

00:22:13.427 --> 00:22:14.888
and people start paying attention to you.

00:22:14.888 --> 00:22:16.547
So I started getting my first brand deals,

00:22:16.547 --> 00:22:18.863
my first brand deal,

00:22:18.863 --> 00:22:20.955
I think I had around 40,000 subscribers,

00:22:20.955 --> 00:22:23.006
somewhere around there
where I started to get

00:22:23.006 --> 00:22:25.812
on companies' radars where
they wanted to hire me

00:22:25.812 --> 00:22:28.482
to do stuff, get involved
with me, send me products,

00:22:28.482 --> 00:22:30.978
hire me for things and so
when you start to build

00:22:30.978 --> 00:22:33.723
an audience, then you'll start
getting more opportunities.

00:22:33.723 --> 00:22:37.149
I got my book deal mostly because
I have a YouTube audience.

00:22:37.149 --> 00:22:39.485
I get offers to join
companies' Boards of Directors

00:22:39.485 --> 00:22:41.091
because of my YouTube audience,

00:22:41.091 --> 00:22:42.085
things that I never thought of.

00:22:42.085 --> 00:22:43.780
I never started my YouTube
channel trying to get

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:46.422
brand deals or book deals
or joining companies' boards

00:22:46.422 --> 00:22:48.879
or investing into businesses,
was never part of the plan,

00:22:48.879 --> 00:22:51.729
but it happened because
I built an audience.

00:22:51.729 --> 00:22:54.478
So there's a painful
point at the start where

00:22:54.478 --> 00:22:56.716
you're doing it because,
and this is any business,

00:22:56.716 --> 00:22:58.585
by the way, like when you're
starting, it's painful

00:22:58.585 --> 00:23:01.551
to start, you're doing it
for the love and the joy.

00:23:01.551 --> 00:23:02.902
There's no company where you just start

00:23:02.902 --> 00:23:04.660
and you're instantly successful.

00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:07.089
There's a lot of heartache
and pain and blood

00:23:07.089 --> 00:23:09.882
and sweat and working on the
quantity to get to the quality

00:23:09.882 --> 00:23:12.929
that then leads to you
having opportunities.

00:23:12.929 --> 00:23:16.484
If you sell an offline
product, trying to dance salsa,

00:23:16.484 --> 00:23:19.035
YouTube is not our main
focus but when we make

00:23:19.035 --> 00:23:22.127
YouTube videos it helps
promote an offline business,

00:23:22.127 --> 00:23:26.475
like looking at Eric Thomas
who became YouTube famous

00:23:26.475 --> 00:23:29.421
and he turned that into
offline businesses,

00:23:29.421 --> 00:23:32.318
offline revenue streams,
seminars and conferences

00:23:32.318 --> 00:23:34.683
and speaking gigs and I don't
know if he does coaching,

00:23:34.683 --> 00:23:38.311
apparel, books, turned it
into an offline business

00:23:38.311 --> 00:23:41.124
and doesn't focus as much on YouTube.

00:23:41.124 --> 00:23:42.882
So other people have passed
him on the YouTube front,

00:23:42.882 --> 00:23:45.808
but it's okay for him because
he's making money elsewhere.

00:23:45.808 --> 00:23:47.530
So there's a lot of different paths,

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:50.262
but at the start, if you haven't started,

00:23:50.262 --> 00:23:51.884
you're just on your way,
I wouldn't even worry

00:23:51.884 --> 00:23:52.934
about monetizing.

00:23:52.934 --> 00:23:54.133
If just making money is your goal,

00:23:54.133 --> 00:23:55.839
do something else 'cause
it's going to take

00:23:55.839 --> 00:23:57.230
a long time to get there.

00:23:57.230 --> 00:23:59.445
You got to do the videos
because you love them.

00:23:59.445 --> 00:24:01.387
Kyle Dunn, "How important
is production quality

00:24:01.387 --> 00:24:03.569
"of a video, like editing
music, transitions?"

00:24:03.569 --> 00:24:04.687
Kind of talked about it.

00:24:04.687 --> 00:24:07.970
It's important but, sorry,
Christina editing this video,

00:24:07.970 --> 00:24:11.534
it's important, but it's you.

00:24:11.534 --> 00:24:13.261
You could have the best
editing in the world,

00:24:13.261 --> 00:24:15.361
but if your message sucks
and you suck on camera,

00:24:15.361 --> 00:24:17.718
it's not going to save you.

00:24:17.718 --> 00:24:19.962
You would get way better
results is you doing it.

00:24:19.962 --> 00:24:22.423
So don't let those things hold you back.

00:24:22.423 --> 00:24:23.621
Get started, improve your message,

00:24:23.621 --> 00:24:25.714
get better, practice,
practice, practice, practice,

00:24:25.714 --> 00:24:27.827
practice, make a good video.

00:24:27.827 --> 00:24:30.244
Anthony Lazaro, "I think the
million-dollar question is

00:24:30.244 --> 00:24:32.915
"how do you choose the topics
with Google Trends video?"

00:24:32.915 --> 00:24:34.430
I don't use Google Trends.

00:24:34.430 --> 00:24:35.853
I don't use Google Trends at all.

00:24:35.853 --> 00:24:38.993
Most of the topics come from
what you guys are asking for.

00:24:38.993 --> 00:24:41.797
So when I'm doing a Top 10,
when I'm doing Believe Live,

00:24:41.797 --> 00:24:43.573
when I'm doing Mentor Me, they come from

00:24:43.573 --> 00:24:45.942
what you guys have been asking for,

00:24:45.942 --> 00:24:47.546
what's already popular on the channel.

00:24:47.546 --> 00:24:51.141
Our Top 10s, for example,
we have 3,000-ish requests

00:24:51.141 --> 00:24:52.525
for Top 10s to do.

00:24:52.525 --> 00:24:54.719
We look at what the most popular ones are.

00:24:54.719 --> 00:24:56.222
So, what are the names
that have been put up,

00:24:56.222 --> 00:24:58.159
who's been mentioned the most,

00:24:58.159 --> 00:24:58.992
and then we start looking,

00:24:58.992 --> 00:25:00.601
can we get enough content on them.

00:25:00.601 --> 00:25:03.113
Some, there's not enough
content, so we can't do it,

00:25:03.113 --> 00:25:04.501
but that's how we pick it,

00:25:04.501 --> 00:25:07.957
and the topics for other
videos are usually based on

00:25:07.957 --> 00:25:09.391
what you guys are asking for

00:25:09.391 --> 00:25:12.711
or this series, I wanted
to make a video on it.

00:25:12.711 --> 00:25:14.235
Nobody said, hey, make
a video series on how

00:25:14.235 --> 00:25:15.750
to get a million subscribers.

00:25:15.750 --> 00:25:17.010
I just wanted to do it,

00:25:17.010 --> 00:25:18.298
and so it's that combination,

00:25:18.298 --> 00:25:21.579
what the audience is asking
for plus what I'm doing.

00:25:21.579 --> 00:25:25.199
We don't look at Google Trends and say,

00:25:25.199 --> 00:25:27.090
hey, what's happening right now

00:25:27.090 --> 00:25:30.523
and let's try to just ride this wave out.

00:25:30.523 --> 00:25:31.730
It's definitely a model,

00:25:31.730 --> 00:25:34.973
and maybe that's a blind spot for us.

00:25:34.973 --> 00:25:36.670
That's just not how we've
achieved our growth.

00:25:36.670 --> 00:25:38.061
Alright, I think I'm going
to end it there guys.

00:25:38.061 --> 00:25:39.442
Tons of questions came in.

00:25:39.442 --> 00:25:41.401
There's still a lot more to get too,

00:25:41.401 --> 00:25:42.986
but I'm seeing some repeat ones come in.

00:25:42.986 --> 00:25:45.375
So, if you have a question
you want me to answer

00:25:45.375 --> 00:25:47.801
in the next edition of this series,

00:25:47.801 --> 00:25:49.599
leave it down in the comments below.

00:25:49.599 --> 00:25:50.971
If you see questions that you like,

00:25:50.971 --> 00:25:53.238
give them a thumbs up
so I'll see them first

00:25:53.238 --> 00:25:54.701
when I'm making the video next time,

00:25:54.701 --> 00:25:56.387
and if you want this series to continue,

00:25:56.387 --> 00:25:58.141
leave it down below as well.

00:25:58.141 --> 00:25:59.443
Thank you guys for the love.

00:25:59.443 --> 00:26:01.121
Thank you for joining on my journey to hit

00:26:01.121 --> 00:26:02.897
a million subscribers, and
hopefully as I teach you

00:26:02.897 --> 00:26:05.063
in the process, you'll
get strategies to apply

00:26:05.063 --> 00:26:08.076
to your own channel to help
you achieve your goals as well,

00:26:08.076 --> 00:26:10.020
whether it's hitting a million, 100,000,

00:26:10.020 --> 00:26:12.641
10,000, 1,000, 10 million!

00:26:12.641 --> 00:26:14.092
Whatever your subscriber goal is,

00:26:14.092 --> 00:26:15.813
hopefully this series is helping you.

00:26:15.813 --> 00:26:18.016
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Playster.

00:26:18.016 --> 00:26:19.916
Thank you so much for
bringing up a copy of my book,

00:26:19.916 --> 00:26:22.405
Your One Word and sharing it on Twitter,

00:26:22.405 --> 00:26:23.696
really, really means a lot to me.

00:26:23.696 --> 00:26:25.143
I hope you're enjoying it, reading it

00:26:25.143 --> 00:26:26.428
and getting value from it.

00:26:26.428 --> 00:26:27.645
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:26:27.645 --> 00:26:28.771
I believe in you.

00:26:28.771 --> 00:26:30.753
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:26:30.753 --> 00:26:33.026
and whatever your one word is!

00:26:33.026 --> 00:26:35.443
Much love, I'll see you soon.

